 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447247 1069 "q-181311" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447247 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447247 1071 "![](images/26/264828b133192b7fff74cfef0718ec56cf82d638003bb9774c2318cb3ae2cc2c.png)\n\nThe inequality corresponding to the highlighted region shown above is $x${{field-1}}\n$1\\text{ or }x$\n{{field-2}}$4.$" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447247 1072 #uuid "322d7cc1-ec63-5690-b8ff-cb69089ad748" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447247 1074 "The red rays contain all values less than $1$ or greater than $4.$ In addition, \n\n- the open circle at $1$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $1,$ and\n\n- the closed circle at $4$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $4.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x<1$ or $x\\ge 4.$" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447248 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447241 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447248 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447243 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447248 1069 "q-181351" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447248 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447248 1071 "![](images/94/945f83a6af821028b133995ddc13193b325ce9cea7d97c8617532369b570542e.png)\n\nThe inequality corresponding to the highlighted region shown above is $-1${{field-1}}\n$x$\n{{field-2}}$3.$" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447248 1072 #uuid "4c6aaf3a-5087-5971-9f06-dcb66d6db1fe" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447248 1074 "The red segment contains all values between  $-1$ and $3.$ In addition,\n\n- the closed circle at $-1$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $-1,$ while\n\n- the closed circle at $3$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $3.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents  $-1\\le x\\le 3.$" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447249 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447240 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447249 1069 "q-54811" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447249 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447249 1071 "![](images/2a/2ac03455fb1b259e0f31719c613d9f7c3adb50b7d8e96667514abb7c513ed0e3.png)\n\nWhich inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447249 1072 #uuid "7acb590f-26ef-56eb-bc17-cd672b435fa9" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447249 1074 "The red segment contains all values between  $-1$ and $4.$ In addition,\n\n- the closed circle at $-1$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $-1,$ while\n\n- the closed circle at $4$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $4.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents  $-1\\le x\\le 4.$" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447250 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447246 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447250 1069 "q-54814" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447250 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447250 1071 "Which of the following number lines represents the inequality $-4\\le x\\le 0?$" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447250 1072 #uuid "a3a4f7e6-baa5-55ec-a1d3-42158ee1abc0" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447250 1074 "The inequality $-4\\le x\\le 0$ means that $x$ can take any value greater than or equal to $-4,$ and less than or equal to $0.$\n\nTo represent this on a number line, we draw a closed circle at $-4$ and another closed circle at $0.$ Then, we highlight the region between the points.\n\n![](images/e8/e884f5bcda9ad664f00a59c8bffcd72ce21472b2cb9127c26ad5cdbd42c73fc5.png)" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447251 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447244 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447251 1069 "q-28806" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447251 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447251 1071 "Which of the following number lines represents the inequality $x\\le 0$ or $x>\\frac{11}{5}?$" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447251 1072 #uuid "f3147df7-04f3-51f7-bd72-80ab17bf146c" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447251 1074 "The inequality $x\\le 0$ or $x>\\frac{11}{5}$ means that $x$ can take any value less than or equal to $0,$ or greater than  $\\frac{11}{5}.$\n\nTo represent this on a number line, we graph the two separate inequalities:\n\n- the inequality $x\\le 0$ consists of a closed circle at $0$ and an arrow to the left.\n\n- the inequality $x>\\frac{11}{5}$ consists of an open circle at $\\frac{11}{5}$ and an arrow to the right.\n\nThe resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/32/32b854cb4bfa0e9d92e044c22275f9ad7c830f621507ee17838d00f650cfe713.png)" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447252 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447239 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447252 1069 "q-103131" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447252 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447252 1071 "![](images/26/263c58a4250424e5dd87e991e2d2d87656c1fa08d10cfc178637d44d63414423.png)\n\nWhich inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447252 1072 #uuid "fecedee9-3a13-5fd5-818f-649e22887a19" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true] [17592186447252 1074 "The red rays contain all values less than $-2$ or greater than $2.$ In addition, \n\n- the open circle at $-2$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $-2,$ and\n\n- the open circle at $2$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $2.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x<-2$ or $x>2.$" 13194139534995 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-082c1ab0-8e73-591d-8757-8fbc99782912" 17592186447215 "answer-113fb996-f646-5f2c-a2c1-2ddf035922b9" 17592186447216 "answer-1acf19ca-e1ca-52d2-a28d-44666d70c49b" 17592186447217 "answer-1ffbefb9-b444-5dc0-9cde-2b9b8e723e45" 17592186447218 "answer-2213c361-04